  "headline": "Jujutsu Kaisen Beginner's Guide: Everything You Need to Know Before Watching",
  "description": "A beginner-friendly primer for Jujutsu Kaisen covering the world setting, main characters, and recommended watch order.",
  "articleBody": "Jujutsu Kaisen is an anime series based on the manga by Gege Akutami. Since its anime adaptation in 2020, it has become one of the most popular anime worldwide. This guide covers the essentials for first-time viewers.\n\n■ Overview\nHigh schooler Yuji Itadori swallows a cursed object — one of Sukuna's fingers — and is thrust into the world of jujutsu sorcerers. Set around Tokyo Jujutsu High, the story follows sorcerers who battle Cursed Spirits born from human negativity.\n\n■ Main Characters\nYuji Itadori: The protagonist. After becoming Sukuna's vessel, he enrolls at Jujutsu High. Known for his extraordinary physical abilities.\nMegumi Fushiguro: Yuji's classmate. Uses the Ten Shadows Technique to summon shikigami. Calm and analytical.\nNobara Kugisaki: Yuji's classmate. A strong-willed sorcerer who fights using a straw doll and nails.\nSatoru Gojo: Regarded as the strongest jujutsu sorcerer and the students' teacher. Possesses the Limitless technique and Six Eyes.\n\n■ Recommended Watch Order (as of February 2026)\n1. TV Anime Season 1 (24 episodes, 2020): Introduction to the story and core concepts.\n2. Jujutsu Kaisen 0 Movie (2021): A prequel featuring Yuta Okkotsu. Best watched after Season 1.\n3. TV Anime Season 2 (23 episodes, 2023): Covers the Hidden Inventory/Premature Death arc and the Shibuya Incident.\n4. TV Anime Season 3 (2025–): Covers the Culling Game arc.\n\n■ Key Concepts for Beginners\nCursed Energy is generated from negative human emotions and forms the foundation of the series' power system. Each sorcerer has a unique Cursed Technique that defines their fighting style. The story features heavy foreshadowing from early episodes, so paying attention to character relationships enhances the viewing experience.\n\nThis article provides a spoiler-minimal introduction. Detailed episode analyses and character breakdowns are available in separate articles.",
